<section class="row justify-content-center"><div class="col-lg-9">
<h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="text-muted">Last updated: 21 October 2026</p>
<p>This policy explains how Choosery (the storefront service operated through StoreBridge) handles personal information when you visit the platform, register, manage a store, or place an order.</p>
<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Information we collect</h2>
<ul><li>Seller account information, including name, email address, and phone number.</li><li>Store details, products, prices, images, and business contact information you choose to publish.</li><li>Customer order information supplied at checkout, including name, phone number, delivery address, order notes, and order contents.</li><li>Subscription/payment-review details such as plan, sender name, transfer reference, review status, and related audit records. Choosery currently supports manual bank-transfer review; a transfer reference alone is not proof of payment.</li><li>Technical and security information generated by use of the platform, where available, such as account actions and timestamps.</li></ul>
<h2 class="h4 mt-4">How information is used</h2><p>We use information to create and protect accounts, operate storefronts and orders, enable seller-customer contact, administer subscriptions, investigate suspected abuse, provide support, and maintain platform security. We may record registration-risk flags when an attempted registration reuses an email address or phone number already associated with an account. A flag is a review signal, not proof of fraud, and does not by itself establish wrongdoing.</p>
<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Sharing and third parties</h2><p>Customer order details are made available to the relevant seller and may be included in a WhatsApp handoff when the customer chooses to continue there. WhatsApp and other external services process information under their own terms and privacy notices. We do not sell personal information. Information may be disclosed where required by law or where reasonably necessary to protect users, the service, or legal rights.</p>
<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Retention and security</h2><p>We retain information for as long as reasonably necessary to operate accounts, fulfil orders, resolve disputes, meet legal obligations, and maintain security/audit records. We use measures such as access controls, password hashing, prepared database statements, and administrative logging, but no internet service can guarantee absolute security.</p>
<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Your choices and rights</h2><p>Subject to applicable law and verification of identity, you may request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal information, or raise an objection or complaint. Some records may need to be retained for security, legal, accounting, or dispute-resolution purposes. Contact us using the details on the <a href="/contact.php">Contact page</a>.</p>
<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Children and changes</h2><p>Choosery is intended for business users and is not designed for children. We may update this policy as the service changes; the updated version and date will be published here.</p>
<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Applicable framework</h2><p>We aim to handle personal information in accordance with applicable Nigerian data-protection law, including the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023. This page is a service policy, not a substitute for legal advice or a determination of our legal obligations in every circumstance.</p>
<p class="mt-4">Questions or privacy requests: use the contact details on our <a href="/contact.php">Contact page</a>.</p>
